# 1FAN Backend

Backend services for the 1FAN F1 fantasy sports application.

## Overview

The backend manages F1 race data, contests, user contest entries,
driver predictions, race results, points calculation, and leaderboard
generation.

## Core Domain

The application models the following entities:

- Users
- Races
- Drivers
- Teams
- Race Driver Results
- Contests
- Contest Entries
- Driver Rankings

## Contest Workflow

1. Administrators create contests for upcoming races.
2. Users join an available contest.
3. Users submit predicted driver finishing positions.
4. Users select a fastest-lap driver.
5. Race results are recorded after the race.
6. Predictions are compared against actual results.
7. Points are calculated.
8. Contest and season leaderboards are generated.

## Database

PostgreSQL is used for persistent storage.

The database schema is available here:

[View Database Schema](https://drive.google.com/file/d/1NQ86b5C9gCJlp9v4YUk9zInlUuzTvbsP/view?usp=sharing)
